|* ro_ring5 -- ring swing, buffered-output swing, and per-ring supply current
|*
|* Purpose: issue #13 requires that the chosen stage count carry "its own
|* ring-swing measurement at that count, not ro_ring11's", and that the
|* array's supply current be measured or estimated against the README's
|* power rows. This deck is both, at the five-stage count.
|*
|* Why this is not a re-run of #10's campaign (an explicit non-goal). #10
|* measured swing as a BY-PRODUCT of a transient-NOISE jitter run: every
|* stage input carried a trnoise() source, the run was 115 ns at a coarse
|* step, and vmax/vmin were read off a node that was being deliberately
|* perturbed. That is the right way to get sigma_1 and the wrong way to get
|* a swing number, because the injected noise is part of the measured
|* excursion. This deck is deterministic -- no injected sources at all --
|* so the swing it reports is the ring's own steady-state excursion. It
|* also measures three things #10's decks could not report at all:
|*
|*   1. the BUFFERED output swing (v(rob)), which is what the XOR tree and
|*      the liveness taps actually see. The internal ring node is
|*      slew-limited by the starve device; ro_buf is an unstarved
|*      minimum-width inverter whose job is to square that up. Whether it
|*      succeeds is the question that decides whether a 0.81 x Vdd ring
|*      node is a problem or a non-problem.
|*   2. the running ring's own average supply current at its own vddr pin.
|*      design/README.md's `lstv` row says in as many words that "no sky130
|*      power measurement exists -- the campaign measured jitter and swing,
|*      not supply current". This closes that for the ring.
|*   3. the STOPPED ring's static supply current, from a second, identical
|*      ring instance held at en = 0. That is the per-ring idle figure the
|*      README's idle-current row needs, and it is also the quantitative
|*      basis for the per-ring-supply liveness monitor the array's own
|*      schematic text block describes ("a stopped ring's supply current
|*      collapses"): the ratio of the two currents measured here is the
|*      contrast that monitor would have to resolve.
|*
|* Topology. Two five-stage rings of identical geometry, each on its own
|* supply source so each supply current is separately measurable, built in
|* place from ro_nand2 + 4 x ro_stage exactly as design/xschem/ro_ring5.sch
|* wires them (the same in-place construction #10's jitter decks use, for
|* the same reason: it keeps the injected/observed nodes addressable at the
|* top level). Ring A is enabled and free-running; ring B is held stopped at
|* en = 0. Ring A's output drives one ro_buf on the separate block supply
|* vdd, mirroring design/xschem/ro_array_core.sch's per-ring output buffer,
|* so the buffer's own current never contaminates either ring's vddr.
|*
|* Included netlist: design/ro_array_core.spice via --ro-ring5 (that is the
|* committed, netlist.py --check-guarded library defining ro_nand2,
|* ro_stage and ro_buf; design/ro_ring5.spice does not define ro_buf).
|*
|* PVT: four (temp, supply) points, each bundling the tt/ss/ff process axis:
|*   -40 degC / 1.62 V   the measured entropy-binding corner (ss)
|*    27 degC / 1.80 V   nominal
|*   125 degC / 1.98 V   where #10 measured the five-stage ring's WORST
|*                       swing anywhere in its 27-point grid (0.809 x Vdd,
|*                       at ff) -- the point issue #13's test plan names
|*                       explicitly
|*   -40 degC / 1.98 V   the fastest ring measured anywhere in that grid
|*                       (ff, T_0 = 1.32 ns), which is the point the XOR
|*                       combining node has the hardest time following
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /home/ubuntu/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* ff, /home/ubuntu/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-13/design/ro_array_core.spice, -40.0, 1.62 and 5p. As committed it
|* is not a runnable deck.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/home/ubuntu/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" ff
|
|.include "/home/ubuntu/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-13/design/ro_array_core.spice"
|
|.temp -40.0
|
|* --- ring A: enabled, free-running ------------------------------------
|VddrA vddrA 0 dc 1.62
|VenA enA 0 dc 1.62
|xgA roA enA a1 vddrA 0 ro_nand2 wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x1A a1 a2 vddrA 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x2A a2 a3 vddrA 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x3A a3 a4 vddrA 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x4A a4 roA vddrA 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|
|* --- ring A's output buffer, on the BLOCK supply, not on vddrA ---------
|Vdd vdd 0 dc 1.62
|xbA roA robA vdd 0 ro_buf
|
|* --- ring B: identical geometry, held stopped (en = 0) ------------------
|VddrB vddrB 0 dc 1.62
|VenB enB 0 dc 0
|xgB roB enB b1 vddrB 0 ro_nand2 wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x1B b1 b2 vddrB 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x2B b2 b3 vddrB 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x3B b3 b4 vddrB 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|x4B b4 roB vddrB 0 ro_stage wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|
|.ic v(roA)=0 v(a1)=1.62 v(a2)=0 v(a3)=1.62 v(a4)=0
|
|.tran 5p 80n uic
|
|.control
|run
|* steady-state window: 20 ns of start-up discarded
|meas tran vmax_ring MAX v(roA) from=20n to=80n
|meas tran vmin_ring MIN v(roA) from=20n to=80n
|meas tran vmax_buf MAX v(robA) from=20n to=80n
|meas tran vmin_buf MIN v(robA) from=20n to=80n
|let swing_frac_ring = (vmax_ring - vmin_ring) / 1.62
|let swing_frac_buf = (vmax_buf - vmin_buf) / 1.62
|* period from 8 whole periods, first two rising edges discarded as start-up
|meas tran tc3 when v(roA)=0.5*1.62 rise=3
|meas tran tc11 when v(roA)=0.5*1.62 rise=11
|let tbar = (tc11 - tc3)/8
|* duty cycle of the ring node, at the 50% crossing
|meas tran tfall3 when v(roA)=0.5*1.62 fall=3
|meas tran tc4 when v(roA)=0.5*1.62 rise=4
|let duty_ring = (tfall3 - tc3) / (tc4 - tc3)
|* supply currents. i(Vsrc) is negative for current delivered by the source,
|* so the reported figures are sign-flipped to read as consumed current.
|meas tran iddr_run_raw AVG i(VddrA) from=20n to=80n
|meas tran iddr_stop_raw AVG i(VddrB) from=20n to=80n
|meas tran ibuf_raw AVG i(Vdd) from=20n to=80n
|let i_ring_run = -iddr_run_raw
|let i_ring_stop = -iddr_stop_raw
|let i_buf = -ibuf_raw
|let stop_ratio = i_ring_run / i_ring_stop
|print swing_frac_ring
|print swing_frac_buf
|print vmax_ring
|print vmin_ring
|print tbar
|print duty_ring
|print i_ring_run
|print i_ring_stop
|print i_buf
|print stop_ratio
|.endc
|.end
|

